WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.490
Choose one service you can sell, and get ready safely.

2
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.830
This is the video for module one of Freelancing Fundamentals.

3
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:19.570
A freelancer is a self-employed person who sells a service to several clients. You find the client, agree the job, do it, send the bill and make sure you are paid.

4
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:34.050
Every job passes through six stages: find, pitch, agree, deliver, get paid, and keep the client. Beginners often focus only on doing the work, and are surprised when the money does not come.

5
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:37.240
Not every hour you work is paid.

6
00:00:38.490 --> 00:00:43.420
And clients hire a clear answer to one problem, so you will choose one service first.

7
00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:51.810
A billable hour is an hour of work a client pays for. Finding clients, pitching and invoicing are not billable.

8
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.370
For example, Amaka in Ibadan has two school-age children. Let us count her week.

9
00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:05.620
She can work 5 hours a day on weekdays, plus 2 hours on Saturday. That is 27 working hours a week.

10
00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:11.940
She keeps 1 hour each weekday for finding clients and admin. That is 5 hours.

11
00:01:13.190 --> 00:01:17.520
She allows another 4 hours for unpaid revisions, calls and learning.

12
00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:23.490
So 27 minus 5 minus 4 leaves 18 billable hours a week.

13
00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:29.900
Over about 4 weeks, that is 72 billable hours a month, not 108.

14
00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:34.710
If you price as if every hour is paid, you will earn far less than you planned.

15
00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:44.450
The most common beginner mistake is offering everything. Instead, list skills you have really used, written as tasks someone could pay for.

16
00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:56.430
Next, look for evidence of demand: job sites, local businesses, people in your network, and your WhatsApp groups. Many sellers is a good sign. It proves people buy.

17
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:08.540
Then score each skill from 1 to 5 on skill and on demand. For example, Hauwa in Kaduna found translation scored 9 out of 10, so it became her first service.

18
00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:15.570
Last, write your offer line. I help a specific client get a result they want by my service.

19
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:21.580
Lines like I am a writer, or I do social media, leave the client guessing.

20
00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:35.180
Compare this. I help small online fashion shops sell more by writing clear product descriptions. It names the client, the result and the service, without promising results you cannot control.

21
00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:47.570
A buffer is savings that cover your essential costs while you build clients, so you do not accept bad jobs out of panic. A common rule of thumb is about three months of essentials.

22
00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:55.670
Chioma's essential costs are about 200,000 naira a month. Three months would be 600,000.

23
00:02:56.920 --> 00:03:00.760
But her shop job covers about 150,000 a month.

24
00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.950
So her real gap is only 50,000 a month.

25
00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:18.510
Her buffer is 50,000 times 3, which is 150,000 naira, not 600,000. She saves 25 percent of every freelance payment until it is complete.

26
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:23.920
Scammers follow people looking for work online. Learn three patterns.

27
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:29.730
One. Someone asks you to pay for training or a fee before you start. Real clients pay you.

28
00:03:30.980 --> 00:03:39.470
Two. Someone pays more than agreed, then begs you to refund the extra. The first payment later disappears, and your refund is gone.

29
00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:45.440
Three. Someone asks for the six-digit code sent to your phone. Never share it.

30
00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:51.330
And screenshots are not payment. Start work only when the money shows in your own banking app.

31
00:03:52.580 --> 00:04:05.150
Before you look for clients, run this check. A professional email, two-step verification, a WhatsApp Business profile, cloud storage and a calendar, a backup connection, and a safe payment channel.

32
00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:14.030
To remember. You run a one-person business. Plan income on billable hours. Choose one service with real demand.

33
00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:21.130
Write an offer line that names the client, the result and the service. And never pay to work or share your codes.

34
00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:30.310
Now it is your turn. Map your real working week, test three skills and write your offer line, then complete your readiness check.

35
00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.600
Continue with the lessons below.
